    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow file. The issue was in how the `frai` CLI was delegating to `frai-gate`.\n\n**The fix involved two changes to `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`:**\n\n1. **Added `.enablePositionalOptions(true)`** to the main program (line 604) - This allows the `gate` subcommand to use `passThroughOptions()`\n\n2. **Added `.passThroughOptions(true)`** to the `gate` command (line 741) - This tells commander.js to pass all options (like `--ci`) through to the subprocess without parsing them, ensuring they're included in the args array passed to the gate CLI\n\n**The rebuilt package now correctly:**\n- Creates `FRAI-SPEC.md`\n- Creates `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` with the GitHub Actions workflow content\n\nThe fix ensures that all flags passed to `frai gate` are properly forwarded to the underlying `frai-gate` CLI.",
